.TH shutdown_state 2 2026-11-20 DarqOS "DarqOS Kernel API Manual"
.SH NAME
shutdown_state \- what a shutdown is waiting for
.SH LIBRARY
.I darq
.SH SYNOPSIS
.BR shutdown_state() " -> tuple[bool, list[ShutdownWait]]"
.PP
class \fIShutdownWait\fP:
    dpid: \fIint\fP
    name: \fIstr\fP
    note: \fIstr\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR shutdown_state ()
returns whether a shutdown, or reboot, is running, and the processes it's
waiting for: each one asked to finish, and not yet gone, by its DPID,
its program's path, and the note it last gave, as "saving", with
WAIT.
The Terminal shows them while it's shutting down.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B NotPermittedError
The process isn't a system process: the p-kernel didn't spawn it.
.SH HISTORY
Introduced in \fISecond Edition\fP.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
running, waiting = darq.shutdown_state()
for wait in waiting:
    print(wait.name, wait.note)
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR on_shutdown (3),
.BR shutdown_now (2),
.BR shutdown_state (2),
.BR pkernel (8),
.BR pyloader (8)
